# Line endings for files whose BYTES are compared, not just their text.
#
# Copied from the Aver Engine's .gitattributes (the rules that apply here: the Aver format fixtures under tests/ and test-content/). A machine
# with core.autocrlf=true rewrites checked-out files to CRLF; that is fine for source, but the tests compare the bytes of these files with the
# bytes the converter writes, so a CRLF copy fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the code. Pinned to LF, the comparison means what
# it says everywhere.
*.ocgraph  text eol=lf
*.ocmat    text eol=lf
*.ocmap    text eol=lf
*.ocproject text eol=lf
